  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large ovenproof pan over medium heat. Add the onion and both peppers with a pinch of salt, and cook for 6 to 8 minutes until softened.",
    "Stir in the garlic, then add the potatoes and courgette. Cook for 3 minutes, stirring often, so the vegetables start to pick up some colour.",
    "Add the canned tomatoes, tomato paste, vegetable stock, smoked paprika, oregano, bay leaf, black pepper and chickpeas. Bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Cook uncovered for 18 to 20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the potatoes are tender and the stew has thickened. Add a splash of water if it looks too dry.",
    "Preheat the oven to 200°C.",
    "Taste the stew and adjust the seasoning. Make 4 small hollows in the stew and crack an egg into each one.",
    "Transfer the pan to the oven and bake for 8 to 10 minutes, until the egg whites are set and the yolks are still a little soft, or longer if you prefer them firmer.",
    "Scatter over the chopped parsley and serve straight from the pan with crusty bread, if desired."
